k you to all our  readers and all of our users  so needless to say when we started  writing a book we never expected an  Academy Award would be the end result of  that effort  we'd like to also thank Donald Knuth who  invented this idea of literate  programming and it's this kind of  radical idea actually which is that  computer programs should be written as  much for people to read as for computers  to execute and our book is a literate  program and we think this approach this  technique for kind of introducing ideas  and explaining them has been integral to  whatever impact the book has had so  thanks Don I'd like to thank Deirdre who  famously let me bring the manuscript for  the book on our honeymoon the the far  girls  Sheila Megan who I hope will read this  at some point and my parents are here  today for early encouragement and access  to computing resources thank you you  know the ability to do realistic  lighting simulation has been one of the  dreams of computer graphics for the last  twenty years we just want to acknowledge  some of the pioneers in that field in  particular Turner Whitted Don Greenberg  Jim ghujiya  and ken Torrence who really laid the  foundations for all we did  and finally I want to thank Dowell my  wife who for many years tolerated a copy  of chamber soccer's radio transport  theory on my bedside table every night
 

